      "preview": "**\ud83e\udd4a Tale of the Tape:**  \nJustin Jefferfather\u2019s roster carries a clear edge in both volume and upside, projecting 105.1 points versus T\u2011Mac Attack\u2019s 86.2.  The gap widens dramatically after the Patriots announce RB TreVeyon\u202fHenderson is out, stripping T\u2011Mac of a primary backfield workhorse.\n\n**\ud83d\udd25 The X\u2011Factors:**  \n- **T\u2011Mac Attack:** *Matthew\u202fStafford* (LAR) remains the only viable passer\u2011rush hybrid; his upside hinges on a clean\u2011sheet matchup that forces the opposing secondary into a pass\u2011heavy script, allowing him to exploit his 7.2\u202fY/A rate.  However, the loss of *TreVeyon\u202fHenderson* eliminates a high\u2011volume backfield option, forcing the team to lean on lower\u2011tier RB depth (Cam\u202fSkattebo, Jaylen\u202fWarren, etc.) whose combined carries drop below 30\u202f% of the team\u2019s total rushing attempts.  The WR core (Luther\u202fBurden, Tre\u2019\u202fHarris) must shoulder the bulk of the floor, but neither has a proven slot\u2011target ceiling against a mid\u2011tier defense.  \n\n- **Justin Jefferfather:** *Jalen\u202fHurts* (PHI) is a dual\u2011threat engine with a 5.1\u202fY/A rushing rate and a 260\u2011yard passing ceiling when the defense leans on the run.  His matchup pits him against a secondary that has allowed the 5th\u2011most QB rushing yards this season, guaranteeing a baseline of scrambles and designed runs.  *Dameon\u202fPierce* (PHI) continues to receive a steady share of goal\u2011line carries (\u2248\u202f30\u202f% of PHI\u2019s rushing attempts) and is positioned in a red\u2011zone\u2011friendly scheme that should translate to TD upside.  The WR trio (Drake\u202fLondon, Jalen\u202fCoker, Josh\u202fDowns) provides a balanced three\u2011target spread, with London\u2019s deep\u2011ball volume and Coker\u2019s return from practice confirming full health.\n\n**\ud83d\udd2e The Verdict:**  \n**Justin\u202fJefferfather** defeats **T\u2011Mac\u202fAttack**, 105.1 to 86.2, driven by *Hurts\u2019* dual\u2011threat efficiency and the loss of *Henderson* that collapses T\u2011Mac\u2019s backfield production."
